- Story & Context: Elena, the group’s lead programmer, stands in the shadow of a surveillance tower, trembling as she confesses that her father is the one who installed the city’s kill-switch. She wipes soot from her forehead with a thumb, her hands raw from hours of manual soldering under the steel grates. The fear in her eyes dissolves into manic laughter as she realizes their music has effectively locked the city police out of their own command center. "This is how we hold the gate open."
