Track 3: Paper Planes and Power Lines
- Story & Context: Years after the Great Lockdown, local kids play a game where they toss paper airplanes into the high-voltage cables to see which ones ignite into sparks first. The sky hangs heavy with the history of the riots, but for these children, the hum of the city is just a background lullaby for their impossible, rule-bending childhoods. Old timers say that if you touch the wire while the bass kicks, you can still hear the ghosts of the first protest anthem vibrating through your teeth. "No rules left in the wires above."
